\newlabel{tbl:tmax-t95}{{2}{7}{Fraction of the total relaxation time needed for $95\%$ of agents to learn, $t_{95}/t_{\rm max}$, for the inner corner arrangement. Each entry averages this fraction over 20 runs at each of the ten coupling strengths $\rho _0=0.1,0.2,\dots ,1.0$, since the predicted ratio does not depend on $\rho _0$ (the simulated broadcast values vary by at most $0.03$ across $\rho _0$). The prediction is Eq.~\eqref {eq:tmax-t95} for independently transitioning agents with $\delta \lambda =0$}{table.2}{}}
